  "kids" : [ {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 102,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 34.333, 547.333, 180.333, 742.333 ],
    "font" : "HelveticaNeue-Light",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "No use being a zealot. A couple of teaspoons of sugar on your morning oatmeal or cereal, and beans or greens cooked in a small amount of bacon or ham won’t wreck your routine. Eat just about anything you want or crave (reasonable amounts) for one meal a week. Life without pizza on the weekend would be unendurable for some people. One alcoholic beverage (a beer, glass of wine, or a drink) once a week at mealtime is fine. Any eating plan will fail if it is too rigid."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 122,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 35.667, 525.667, 61.667, 537.667 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "AntiqueOliT-Bold",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.882, 0.231, 0.149]",
    "content" : "Size"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 131,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 34.333, 478.0, 180.333, 514.0 ],
    "font" : "HelveticaNeue-Light",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "You have nothing to lose but fat, and some sizes in your belt and clothes."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 142,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 35.667, 452.333, 78.333, 467.0 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "AntiqueOliT-Bold",
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "text color" : "[0.882, 0.231, 0.149]",
    "content" : "Timing"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 145,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 35.0, 295.667, 179.667, 441.0 ],
    "font" : "HelveticaNeue-Light",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Is this your time for blubber elimination? King Solomon wrote of the proper time for everything under the sun: a time to sow and a time to reap, a time to live and a time to die—and so on. No one will decide to lose fat (or stop being an alcoholic) until the proper time is reached—for him or her. For people who are tortured by being overweight, the time just might be right now. Yours for good health and"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 162,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 35.667, 271.667, 179.667, 297.667 ],
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "Yours for good health and safe flying"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 168,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 35.0, 163.667, 181.0, 263.0 ],
    "font" : "HelveticaNeue-LightItalic",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Dr. Stoutt is a partner in the Springs Pediatrics and Aviation Medicine Clinic, Louisville, Ky., and he has been an active AME since 1960. No longer an active pilot, he holds a commercial pilot’s certificate with instrument, multi-engine, and CFI ratings."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 187,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 35.333, 57.333, 181.0, 153.0 ],
    "font" : "HelveticaNeue-LightItalic",
    "font size" : 10.0,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Note: This article appeared in the Summer 2002 Federal Air Surgeon’s Medical Bulletin . The views and recommendations made in this article are those of the author and not necessarily those of the Federal Aviation Administration."
